(* Blorp 2: local selective function imports, scalar bindings, fixed unions and
   records, tail matches, ordinary type selections and an explicit target library.

   This is a byte-level source grammar. No whitespace is implicit.
   Dialect: `=` defines a rule; `;` ends it; juxtaposition concatenates;
   `|` means alternatives; (...) groups; [...] is zero or one occurrence;
   {...} is zero or more occurrences; quoted strings are literal bytes;
   "A".."Z" is an inclusive single-byte range; comments use parentheses
   around asterisks. X - Y excludes the complete strings of Y from X.
   Grammar literal escapes are \n = LF (0x0A), \r = CR (0x0D), \t = TAB (0x09),
   \" = double quote (0x22), and \xNN = the byte with hexadecimal value NN.
   These grammar-literal escapes do not introduce source escapes.
   EOF succeeds only at the exact end of the source, consuming no byte.

   Lexical contracts:
   - Identifiers use the longest consecutive identifier byte run.
   - The exact spellings `func`, `pure`, `match`, `var`, `void`, and `_` are reserved.
     Lone `_` is a wildcard token; `_name` remains an identifier.
   - Integer tokens use the longest consecutive digit run, with an optional
     adjacent minus. Parsing rejects leading zeros and values outside
     -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807. `-0` has value zero.
   - Source Float uses decimal digits with a fraction or exponent, no leading
     zeros, separators, hexadecimal forms or suffixes. Fractions need digits on
     both sides of the dot; exponent digits follow optional +/- immediately.
     Source overflow is rejected; subnormals and underflow to signed zero are
     accepted. Plus signs, separated minus signs and arithmetic operators are
     unsupported. A dot followed by a digit belongs to a Float token; other dots
     retain UFCS/field syntax, including `42.identity()` and `1.5.identity()`.
     A dot directly after an integer must be followed by fraction digits or,
     after optional spaces, a field or function name.
   - Arrow bytes stay adjacent. Spaces occur only where these rules permit.
   - Identifiers and comments remain ASCII; quoted values admit valid UTF-8.
     CR is unsupported as a raw byte, including in comments and quotes.
   - Quoted String values occupy one physical line. Nine fixed escapes and
     \u{H} with one to six hexadecimal digits are accepted. Unicode escapes
     must denote scalars through 10FFFF, excluding D800..DFFF. Raw UTF-8 must
     use shortest scalar encodings. No normalization occurs. Length and spans
     count bytes. Raw ASCII controls and DEL are unsupported inside quotes.
   - `--` starts a single-line comment ending before LF or EOF. It takes
     precedence over a signed integer; `->` still forms an arrow.
   - Blank, whitespace-only and comment-only lines are lexical trivia. Their
     indentation has no layout meaning. Only lines containing code produce
     layout tokens, retaining their original byte offsets (see Layout below).

   Syntax accepts any unreserved function, parameter and type identifier.
   `import`, `fixed`, `union`, and `record` are contextual words in module headers, and remain
   valid function, type, parameter and variant identifiers elsewhere.
   Import blocks precede the module's declarations and select functions by their declared names from explicit ./ or leading
   ../ paths, or bare paths under an explicitly supplied target-library root.
   Paths omit .brp and contain adjacent identifier components; interior
   dot segments, aliases, wildcards and reexports are unsupported. Explicit
   Union(First, Second) imports select a union and named constructors; Union()
   selects its type alone. Bare names resolve functions or visible types without capitalization rules.
   A type selection supplies target-local receiver functions for UFCS. The contextual
   suffix methods_only supplies receiver functions without importing the type or constructors.
   All declarations are public. Foundation types and constructors are implicit in
   every module. User modules also receive the ordinary foundation prelude's
   selected UFCS operations; library operations receive only base and written imports.
   Every declaration has a program-wide identity and a defining module. Imports
   preserve that identity. Bodies and annotations resolve in their defining
   module. Import dependency cycles are accepted. Each source is loaded once.
   The checker requires exactly one nongeneric root-local `main` returning Int or Void,
   with no parameters or one List[String] parameter. Index 0 is the executable name.
   An omitted return annotation means Void. A pure function cannot return Void,
   including a generic instance whose concrete return type is Void.
   Int main returns its result as the process exit status; Void main exits 0.
   Helper parameter and return types are `Int`, `Float`, `String`, `Void`, List[String] (or List[T] in a generic helper), a declared fixed union,
   a declared fixed record, or one of the function's declared rigid type parameters. Type parameters start
   with a capital ASCII letter and contain only ASCII letters and digits.
   Their names cannot collide with builtin or declared union/record type names.
   Every body is checked once, including unused generic declarations. Only
   all synthesized argument types consistently infer a generic call; expected result types
   do not infer it. Explicit arguments whose receiving annotations contain rigid
   parameters need already-typed union values or concrete helpers. Concrete
   explicit annotations supply constructor context even in generic contracts.
   A generic UFCS receiver receives no constructor hint, even for a concrete
   first annotation. Zero-argument and phantom
   generic calls cannot infer all their parameters. Root-local main and runtime builtin
   declarations cannot be generic. Explicit call type arguments are deferred.
   Fixed unions may declare ordered type parameters. Written applications take ordered
   recursive type arguments: Int, Float, String, Void, in-scope parameters, records, ordinary
   unions or further applications. Payload annotations are Int or one of the
   union's own parameters; concrete payloads specialize to Int, Float, String, Void, an existing
   inline record, or another finite inline union with an earlier concrete layout.
   String-bearing inline unions own their active child path without an allocated
   aggregate root. Recursive layouts and managed record fields remain unsupported.
   Phantom String applications remain valid. Instance identity includes the
   declaration and complete ordered concrete arguments, independently of layout.
   Type names occupy a separate module-local namespace from function and variant names.
   Union type names and variants within one union must be unique. Functions
   cannot share a variant name; variants in different unions may share names.
   Bare variants resolve in the expected union type, determined by the
   receiving function parameter or declared return type. A local parameter
   shadows a same-named variant or direct call and cannot be called. A UFCS
   target resolves in the containing module, independently of parameter shadowing; its receiver
   uses the containing function's scope. Calls require matching arity and
   nominal types, and pure callers calling only pure callees. Self and mutual
   function recursion are accepted. Generic call substitutions must not contain
   a parameter-dependency cycle that nests a parameter inside an application;
   bare-parameter permutations and paths ending in concrete resets remain finite.
   Unannotated calls use the ordinary C stack, without a constant-stack guarantee.
   A single @tail_recursive before optional pure/func requires nongeneric direct
   self recursion, with every self call in a whole function or match-arm tail.
   Direct and final UFCS self calls become explicit loop backedges at -O0.
   Arguments, receivers, binding initializers, scrutinees, constructor/record
   children and earlier postfix operations are non-tail. The signature and
   every evaluated value must be unmanaged, including unused initializers.
   Phantom String type arguments without managed payload are allowed.
   Zero-argument annotated helpers and main are allowed; termination is not proved.
   Annotations without direct self calls, generic annotations, and annotations
   on builtin bodies are rejected. Mutual calls remain ordinary calls. Recursive
   data declarations remain unsupported; cyclic runtime value graphs are forbidden.
   Functions without pure are impure. Nullary variants are bare values. A
   variant with one declared field uses unary construction syntax. Constructor
   application is pure and is not a function call; constructor UFCS is deferred.
   Bindings, reassignments and expression statements share one source order.
   A non-final bare expression must return Void; other values must be bound
   or returned. Void has exactly one value, `void`, and is unmanaged in every
   value position. A final expression remains mandatory, even for Void functions.
   A Void function evaluates and discards its final expression (of any type),
   including each selected match-arm result, and returns the sole Void value.
   Discarded expressions still undergo ordinary name, type and purity checking.
   Matches follow any statement prefix and occupy the function tail. Their scrutinee must synthesize
   a union type from a binding or function result; a constructor alone does not
   provide a receiving type. An unshadowed constructor spelling selects that
   union's variant. Other bare names, including a spelling shadowed by a local
   binding, introduce fresh whole-value bindings. Field binders and wildcards
   are irrefutable. Checking requires
   exhaustive, useful arms and type-checks every arm result.
   Bindings resolve initializer names before adding a new local. `var`
   creates a mutable local and may shadow an enclosing binding. Ordinary `=`
   reassigns a visible mutable binding, rejects a visible immutable binding,
   or creates a new immutable local. Duplicate declarations within one block
   are rejected. New local types are inferred; reassignment retains the established
   type. Bare constructors need a receiving type. Every initializer is
   checked and evaluated, even when its binding is unused. An arm may contain
   an inline expression or a depth-three block of statements and a final value.
   Arm-local declarations do not enter sibling scopes. Explicit var may
   shadow an enclosing binding; a second declaration in the same block fails.
   Fixed records are nonempty and nongeneric, with Int fields only. Their type
   names share the builtin/union type namespace; fields are unique within each
   record. Literals require a concrete expected nominal record, contain each
   field exactly once, and evaluate in written order. Empty literals parse but
   fail checking for missing fields. Field reads have no parentheses; UFCS calls
   have parentheses. Only an immediate first nongeneric UFCS call provides a
   base literal hint; a field read supplies none. Generic substitutions never
   contextualize a later explicit argument. Copies and whole-value reassignment
   retain value semantics. Managed/recursive/generic/empty record declarations,
   record updates, field assignment and multiline braces remain unsupported.
   Compiler-known builtin type syntax is parsed in ordinary modules and checked
   only in the configured _base/types.brp foundation role. That module owns Int,
   Float, String, Void and unary List exactly once, plus ordinary Bool/Option/Result
   unions. It imports nothing and declares no functions. _base/prelude.brp is an
   ordinary module of type imports. These designated inputs cannot be imported
   explicitly. No runtime-name fallback or positional prelude input remains.
   Closed builtin bodies are allowed as the sole body of nongeneric module
   functions, without statements or tail annotations. A closed builtin label
   establishes the operation identity and ordinary checking validates its contract.
   Ordinary quoted expressions construct fresh owned String values. Builtin
   declarations match their quoted raw label exactly, without escape decoding.
   In module bodies, builtin is contextual: builtin followed by an opening
   parenthesis and quoted label selects the intrinsic form. Calls builtin()
   and builtin(value) remain ordinary calls to a declared function.
   The pure string.parse_int builtin explicitly selects its payload and empty
   constructors. Checking accepts their declaration identity and exact Int
   payload/empty coverage; specialization translates to concrete identities.
   string.parse_float binds Float payload/empty roles in the same ordinary union.
   Its counted decimal input permits a leading sign and zeros, rejects nonfinite
   or overflowing values, and preserves subnormals and signed zero on underflow.
   Float arithmetic is binary64, with zero divisors returning positive zero.
   float.to_string produces round-trip decimal text using 6..17 significant digits
   and canonical nan/inf/-inf/-0 spellings. No locale or rounding mode is changed.
   Option remains an ordinary library union. Int conversion consumes counted ASCII
   bytes completely and rejects whitespace, NUL, suffixes and Int64 overflow.
   Ownership admits borrowed managed parameters and fresh arm-local managed values
   in a tail match. Prefix definitions introduce no owned obligation, even one
   discharged before the match. Each arm drops its unused/intermediate owners
   or transfers its managed result. Payload extraction borrows the selected
   immutable parent value and acquires returned children independently. Owned
   outer dependencies, nested/non-tail matches and joins remain deferred.
*)

letter           = "A".."Z" | "a".."z" ;
digit            = "0".."9" ;
identifier_start = letter | "_" ;
identifier_byte  = identifier_start | digit ;
identifier       = (identifier_start { identifier_byte }) - ("func" | "pure" | "match" | "var" | "void" | "_") ;

space            = " " ;
spaces           = { space } ;
required_spaces  = space spaces ;
ascii_byte       = "\x00".."\x7F" ;
comment_byte     = ascii_byte - ("\n" | "\r") ;
line_comment     = "--" { comment_byte } ;
horizontal       = space | "\t" ;
trivia_line      = { horizontal } [ line_comment ] ( "\n" | EOF ) ;
indentation      = { "\t" } | { "    " } ;

(* Layout. The lexer turns line structure into the tokens NEWLINE, INDENT and
   DEDENT, which the rules below use instead of LF bytes and indentation.
   - Trivia lines produce no tokens. Every other line is a code line: an
     indentation prefix, then code. The prefix's level is its tab count or its
     count of four-space groups; any other prefix is an error.
   - Every code line ends with NEWLINE: its trailing spaces and optional
     comment, then its LF, or EOF when the source ends without one.
   - A code line one level deeper than the previous code line starts with
     INDENT. Opening more than one level at once is an error, so the open
     levels are always 0 through the current one. A shallower code line starts
     with one DEDENT for each level it closes, and EOF closes every open level.
   - INDENT and DEDENT span the line's indentation prefix; at EOF they and
     the final NEWLINE are empty spans at the end of the source.
   Blocks nest by INDENT and DEDENT alone; no rule names a depth. *)
NEWLINE          = spaces [ line_comment ] ( "\n" | EOF ) ;
INDENT           = indentation ;
DEDENT           = indentation ;

(* A function has one header followed by zero or more ordered statement lines and a
   mandatory expression line or tail match. A union has one header and one or more
   variant lines. An inline comment does not continue an expression onto a later
   code line. Spaces in a call are explicit, including f ( ) and 1 . f ( ). UFCS
   supplies its receiver as the first argument, followed by the ordered explicit
   arguments in its parentheses. All expressions stay on one line, including
   scrutinees and arm results. A match occurs only as a function's tail, and an
   arm block holds statements and a final value, so blocks finish with a
   single-line value and matches do not nest. Non-final expression statements
   must have Void type. Void has the sole value void. A Void function evaluates
   and discards its final expression before returning void. *)
nonzero_digit    = "1".."9" ;
integer          = [ "-" ] ("0" | nonzero_digit { digit }) ;
exponent         = ("e" | "E") [ "+" | "-" ] digit { digit } ;
float            = integer (("." digit { digit } [ exponent ]) | exponent) ;
hex_digit        = digit | "A".."F" | "a".."f" ;
unicode_escape   = "u{" hex_digit [ hex_digit [ hex_digit [ hex_digit [ hex_digit [ hex_digit ] ] ] ] ] "}" ;
string_escape    = "\\" ("n" | "r" | "t" | "0" | "\\" | "\"" | "'" | "{" | "}" | unicode_escape) ;
utf8_tail        = "\x80".."\xBF" ;
utf8_scalar      = "\xC2".."\xDF" utf8_tail
                 | "\xE0" "\xA0".."\xBF" utf8_tail
                 | ("\xE1".."\xEC" | "\xEE".."\xEF") utf8_tail utf8_tail
                 | "\xED" "\x80".."\x9F" utf8_tail
                 | "\xF0" "\x90".."\xBF" utf8_tail utf8_tail
                 | "\xF1".."\xF3" utf8_tail utf8_tail utf8_tail
                 | "\xF4" "\x80".."\x8F" utf8_tail utf8_tail ;
string_byte      = "\x20".."\x21" | "\x23".."\x5B" | "\x5D".."\x7E" | utf8_scalar ;
string_contents  = { string_byte | string_escape } ;
(* Raw interpolation openers are excluded; $\{ remains literal text. *)
string_literal   = "\"" (string_contents - (string_contents "${" string_contents)) "\"" ;
arguments        = expression { spaces "," spaces expression } ;
direct_call      = identifier spaces "(" spaces [ arguments ] spaces ")" ;
record_field     = identifier spaces "=" spaces expression ;
record_literal   = "{" spaces [ record_field { spaces "," spaces record_field } ] spaces "}" ;
primary          = "void" | float | integer | string_literal | identifier | direct_call | record_literal ;
receiver_call    = spaces "." spaces identifier spaces "(" spaces [ arguments ] spaces ")" ;
field_read       = spaces "." spaces identifier ;
expression       = primary { receiver_call | field_read } ;
type_annotation  = identifier spaces [ "[" spaces type_annotation { spaces "," spaces type_annotation } spaces "]" ] ;
parameter        = identifier spaces ":" spaces type_annotation ;
type_parameter   = "A".."Z" { letter | digit } ;
type_parameters = "[" spaces type_parameter { spaces "," spaces type_parameter } spaces "]" spaces ;
function_header  = [ "pure" required_spaces ] "func" required_spaces identifier spaces [ type_parameters ] "(" spaces
                   [ parameter { spaces "," spaces parameter } ] spaces ")" spaces [ "->" spaces type_annotation spaces ] ":"
                   NEWLINE ;
tail_annotation  = "@tail_recursive" (required_spaces | NEWLINE) ;
function         = [ tail_annotation ] function_header INDENT body DEDENT ;
field_pattern    = "_" | identifier ;
pattern          = "_" | identifier spaces [ "(" spaces [ field_pattern ] spaces ")" ] ;
binding          = [ "var" required_spaces ] identifier spaces "=" spaces expression NEWLINE ;
statement        = binding | expression NEWLINE ;
arm_block        = { statement } expression NEWLINE ;
match_arm        = pattern spaces ":" (spaces expression NEWLINE | NEWLINE INDENT arm_block DEDENT) ;
match_body       = "match" required_spaces expression spaces ":" NEWLINE INDENT match_arm { match_arm } DEDENT ;
tail             = expression NEWLINE | match_body ;
body             = { statement } tail | builtin_body ;
variant          = identifier spaces [ "(" spaces identifier spaces ")" ] NEWLINE ;
fixed_union      = "fixed" required_spaces "union" required_spaces identifier spaces [ type_parameters ] ":"
                   NEWLINE INDENT variant { variant } DEDENT ;
record_member    = identifier spaces ":" spaces type_annotation ;
fixed_record     = "fixed" required_spaces "record" required_spaces identifier spaces "{" spaces
                   record_member { spaces "," spaces record_member } spaces "}" NEWLINE ;
declaration      = function | fixed_union | fixed_record | builtin_type ;
relative_prefix  = "./" | "../" { "../" } ;
module_components = identifier { "/" identifier } ;
module_path      = [ relative_prefix ] module_components ;
constructor_selection = spaces "(" spaces [ identifier { spaces "," spaces identifier } ] spaces ")" ;
import_symbol    = identifier [ constructor_selection | required_spaces "methods_only" ] ;
import_selection = import_symbol { spaces "," spaces import_symbol } ;
import_row       = module_path spaces ":" spaces import_selection NEWLINE ;
import_block     = "import" spaces ":" NEWLINE INDENT import_row { import_row } DEDENT ;
program          = { import_block } { declaration } EOF ;

(* Foundation declarations use the ordinary module parser.
   An empty module parses; designated foundation validation requires five builtins. *)
builtin_type     = "type" required_spaces (("Int" | "Float" | "String" | "Void") spaces
                   | "List" spaces "[" spaces identifier spaces "]" spaces) "=" spaces "builtin" NEWLINE ;
builtin_label    = "\"int.to_string\"" | "\"string.length\"" | "\"string.print\""
                   | "\"int.add\"" | "\"int.subtract\"" | "\"int.multiply\""
                   | "\"int.divide\"" | "\"int.remainder\""
                   | "\"float.add\"" | "\"float.subtract\"" | "\"float.multiply\""
                   | "\"float.divide\"" | "\"float.remainder\"" | "\"float.to_string\""
                   | "\"list.length\"" ;
union_builtin    = ("\"string.parse_int\"" | "\"string.parse_float\"" | "\"list.get\"" | "\"int.equals\"" | "\"string.equals\"")
                   spaces "," spaces identifier spaces "," spaces identifier ;
builtin_body     = "builtin" spaces "(" spaces (builtin_label | union_builtin) spaces ")" NEWLINE ;
